## Hardware-native source installer

From version 0.1.2, the independently released `filesystem-exfat-VERSION-native-installer.run`
contains the exact committed source and supports `--profile aggressive --system-package-mode`.
It builds for the local CPU with `-O3 -march=native -mtune=native -flto`,
trains real exFAT operations using the existing independent-media test,
then rebuilds the final freestanding driver using the measured GCC PGO profile.
An unsuccessful training or missing profile fails the installation; never claims
PGO when training has not occurred. The temporary training binary and Linux libc
are **not** installed. Exactly one exFAT.so and one illustrated exFAT.pdf are
owned by the final Debian package; hashes, flags and source revision are recorded
in its Debian control fields. A separate published pinned-kernel KO remains unchanged.
